1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,887
My Mac says I have eighty gigs of System Data.

2
00:00:02,887 --> 00:00:04,441
I did not put it there.

3
00:00:04,591 --> 00:00:07,247
And Storage settings won't tell me what it is.

4
00:00:07,397 --> 00:00:08,836
So I asked Noah.

5
00:00:08,936 --> 00:00:12,192
Noah doesn't guess. It checks the folders on this Mac,

6
00:00:12,192 --> 00:00:15,721
and found it: old caches and leftovers nobody uses.

7
00:00:15,921 --> 00:00:18,480
Here's the part I like: it shows the plan first.

8
00:00:18,580 --> 00:00:21,200
Nothing's deleted. It all goes to the Trash.

9
00:00:21,250 --> 00:00:23,030
And every change is in the log.

10
00:00:23,230 --> 00:00:26,306
Forty-one gigs back. My files didn't change.

11
00:00:26,506 --> 00:00:28,559
Noah for Mac. Free to start.

12
00:00:28,759 --> 00:00:30,768
Now... what's your System Data at?
